ample solution, and the heterogeneous mixtures were shook for 96 h before centrifuging at 7000 rpm for 1 min to achieve phase separation. The final absorbance of the aqueous phase at the λmax of each compound was determined, and their water–octanol partition coefficients were calculated. The experiment was repeated for 6 in 0.6% w/v NaCl solution instead of ddH2O. All experiments were done in triplicate."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"RAS-1T","value":-0.85,"value_relation":"=","std":0.02,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1039/c6sc00268d","year":2016,"counterion":"[Cl-]","record_id":"MLDB-001135","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"Log Pow of RAS-1H an RAS-1T were determined using the shake flask method. RAS-1H and RAS-1T were predissolved in ddH2O that was presaturated with n-octanol (for 24 h and left to stand until phase separation occurs). The UV-vis spectrums for each samples were obtained and the absorbances at the λmax of each compound were determined. Equal volume of n-octanol was added to each sample solution and the heterogeneous mixtures shaked for 2 h before centrifuging at 4000 rpm for 1 min to achieve phase separation. The final absorbance of the aqueous phase at the λmax of each compound were determined and their water-octanol partition coefficient were calculated."}]}